# Agent Skills (this project)

Skills from [addyosmani/agent-skills](https://github.com/addyosmani/agent-skills). Source commit in `.cursor/agent-skills-source/VERSION`.

## Always active

| Rule | When it applies |
|------|-----------------|
| `incremental-implementation` | Multi-file changes — thin vertical slices, verify each step |
| `test-driven-development` | Behavior changes — red/green/refactor, Prove-It pattern |
| `git-workflow-and-versioning` | All commits — atomic, ~100-line changes, trunk-based |
| `security-and-hardening` | Auth, child/parent data, APIs, storage — OWASP, secrets, boundaries |

## Load on demand (mention in chat or open matching files)

| Rule | When to invoke |
|------|----------------|
| `spec-driven-development` | New feature or significant change — write PRD before code |
| `code-review-and-quality` | Before merge — five-axis review, change sizing |
| `debugging-and-error-recovery` | Tests fail, builds break, unexpected runtime behavior |
| `api-and-interface-design` | Backend API work (`backend/**` auto-attaches) |

## How to use

Tell the agent explicitly when you want a workflow, e.g.:

- "Follow spec-driven-development before implementing this feature"
- "Review this diff using code-review-and-quality"
- "Debug this using debugging-and-error-recovery"

To add more skills, copy from the upstream repo into `.cursor/rules/` as `.mdc` files (see upstream `docs/cursor-setup.md`).
